a1671c031f587b8da6f3383352eb191093c348bc5f38c462c4f2","event_uuid":"de3b7a4c-9a4f-4e40-9f21-916f0aac1087","position":{"commit_sha":"2eea222396361e42e131e0d0c29ee29693763a5a","position":"1785980305098409001-de3b7a4c-9a4f-4e40-9f21-916f0aac1087"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Review remediation: this story now depends on 28cd and extends its shared Ruff ratchet test. ACs deterministically parse per-file-ignores to reject every RUF selector/code, assert exact S-family absence, and assert the absent Semgrep configuration baseline instead of relying on diff inspection.","timestamp":1784504674478887001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Review remediation from the latest signed-review candidate: measured 142 actionable RUF diagnostics on Ruff 0.15.19 and separated them from 771 narrow-selection RUF100 artifacts; pinned the deferral to [tool.ruff.lint].ignore with exact RUF001-003 values and no extend-ignore; removed the nonexistent extend-select reference; and removed duplicate S/Semgrep ACs already owned by predecessor 28cd. No production code was changed.","timestamp":1784517689642183001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Post-remediation RUF census (Ruff 0.16.1, current origin/main df34119e02).\n\nSTARTING live narrow census (ruff check --select RUF --ignore RUF001,RUF002,RUF003,RUF100 --statistics src/rebar tests) = 179 actionable diagnostics: RUF059=68, RUF022=38, RUF012=26, RUF005=20, RUF043=12, RUF023=6, RUF007=2, RUF028=2, RUF034=2, RUF019=1, RUF046=1, RUF102=1.\n\nRemediation: Ruff safe --fix (39) + reviewed unsafe --fix for the mechanical families (RUF059 unused-unpacked -> _prefix; RUF005 concat -> unpacking; RUF007 zip -> itertools.pairwise; RUF046 cast; RUF022/RUF023 sorted __all__/__slots__; RUF019/RUF102). Manual: RUF012 -> typing.ClassVar[...] annotations (26, all test stub classes); RUF043 -> raw-string match= patterns (12, byte-identical regex); RUF028 -> removed 2 invalid in-arglist fmt-suppression comments; RUF034 -> collapsed 2 useless if-else. RUF001/RUF002/RUF003 deferred in [tool.ruff.lint].ignore (intentional prose/UI Unicode).\n\nPOST-remediation narrow census = 0 (ruff check --select RUF --ignore RUF001,RUF002,RUF003,RUF100 src/rebar tests exits 0).\n\nAUTHORITATIVE RUF100 under the FULL configured rule set: 'ruff check src tests' exits 0 (All checks passed). Enabling RUF activated RUF100 tree-wide, surfacing 374 genuinely-stale noqa directives (124 unused BLE001 on handlers ruff exempts via logging/re-raise; 59 redundant T201 in per-file-ignored paths; ANN001/ANN201/ANN2xx, F401/F811/F841, E402, PLC0415, PT011, S3xx/S1xx, ARG, N8xx, D1xx, B017) which were removed via ruff's precise RUF100 autofix. The 771 narrow-selection RUF100 artifacts were NOT used to drive removals (per plan). make lint exits 0; default test tier: 10747 passed (only pre-existing host-environmental failures: safe.bareRepository git-remote tests + metric-backend tool absent, each reproduced on the clean tree).","timestamp":1785980305098409001}],"created_at":1784487804685664001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"998bbd47-4c68-406e-aac3-d0619d8a65bb","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"28cd-d8f8-4456-482c"},{"link_uuid":"817c5d1f-929f-4397-b615-4b33e9ccf9e0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"73a4-937a-5583-4ccd"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAt plan authoring (commit 0f5dbc88b, Ruff 0.15.19) the narrow RUF command `ruff check --select RUF --ignore RUF001,RUF002,RUF003,RUF100 --statistics src/rebar tests` reported 142 actionable diagnostics (49 RUF059, 36 RUF022, 18 RUF005, 18 RUF012, 10 RUF043, 6 RUF023, 2 RUF028, and one each of RUF019, RUF046, RUF102). Those figures are dated observations, not the contract. The pinned Ruff is now `ruff==0.16.1` (`pyproject.toml`); the authoritative inventory is whatever that same narrow command reports against the **current** `origin/main` tip. Running the narrow census without ignoring RUF100 also surfaces RUF100 diagnostics that are narrow-selection artifacts (the valid `noqa` codes are outside that command's selected rules); they are not counted as remediation debt.\n\nThis story clears the live narrow-census RUF diagnostics (142 at plan authoring; use the current `origin/main` count) before selecting the family. RUF001, RUF002, and RUF003 remain deferred because many flagged Unicode symbols are intentional prose or UI content. True RUF100 findings are evaluated only with the final full configured rule set after RUF is selected; any suppression that is stale under that full configuration is removed.\n\n## Dependencies and Ownership\nThis story depends on `28cd-d8f8-4456-482c`. The dependency is both ordering and shared-file ownership: the predecessor lands the ASYNC/DTZ `pyproject.toml` configuration and creates `tests/unit/test_ruff_ratchet.py`; this story then edits the resulting configuration and extends that test. It does not create a competing version of the file.\n\n## Approach\n1. Extend `tests/unit/test_ruff_ratchet.py` to require `RUF` in `[tool.ruff.lint].select`.\n2. Add `[tool.ruff.lint].ignore = [\"RUF001\", \"RUF002\", \"RUF003\"]` in `pyproject.toml`. The global deferral lives only in this exact key; do not introduce `extend-ignore` or RUF entries in `per-file-ignores`.\n3. In the shared test, assert that the parsed `ignore` value is exactly the three-item deferral set and that `extend-ignore` is absent. Parse `tool.ruff.lint.per-file-ignores` and assert that no configured code equals `RUF` or starts with `RUF`. This deterministically prohibits broad or code-specific RUF per-file exemptions.\n4. Use the pinned Ruff fixer only for safe mechanical edits, review every diff, then manually resolve remaining enabled RUF diagnostics across `src/rebar` and `tests`. The live narrow census against current `origin/main` is the starting inventory; the implementation records the post-fix per-code census on the ticket.\n5. After RUF is in the global selection, run `ruff check src tests` and remove only RUF100 suppressions that are stale under that full configured rule set. Do not use the narrow-selection RUF100 count to drive removals.\n\nRuff security-family expansion and Semgrep expansion remain deferred and are already guarded by the predecessor's shared ratchet test; this story does not duplicate those orthogonal acceptance criteria.\n\nRejected: RUF per-file ignores, `extend-ignore`, Ruff S-family expansion, Semgrep expansion, and treating narrow-selection RUF100 output as actionable debt.\n\n## Scope\n- `pyproject.toml`\n- `tests/unit/test_ruff_ratchet.py` (extend the file landed by 28cd)\n- source and test files among the diagnostics reported live by the baseline command against current `origin/main`, limited to safe mechanical or behavior-preserving changes\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- Baseline reproduction: `ruff check --select RUF --ignore RUF001,RUF002,RUF003,RUF100 --statistics src/rebar tests`\n- Configuration and deferrals: `pytest -q tests/unit/test_ruff_ratchet.py`\n- Enabled RUF diagnostics: `ruff check --select RUF --ignore RUF001,RUF002,RUF003,RUF100 src/rebar tests`\n- Full configured rule set including authoritative RUF100 evaluation: `ruff check src tests`\n- Canonical lint: `make lint`\n- Default tier: `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -q`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The implementation begins from the live narrow-census inventory measured against current `origin/main` (the baseline command in Context) and changes only files reported by that live census.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_ruff_ratchet.py` asserts `[tool.ruff.lint].select` contains the exact selector `RUF`.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_ruff_ratchet.py` asserts `[tool.ruff.lint].ignore` is exactly `RUF001`, `RUF002`, and `RUF003`.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_ruff_ratchet.py` asserts `[tool.ruff.lint]` has no `extend-ignore` key.\n- [ ] `ruff check --select RUF --ignore RUF001,RUF002,RUF003,RUF100 src/rebar tests` exits 0.\n- [ ] `ruff check src tests` exits 0, proving RUF100 reports no stale `noqa` under the final full configured rule set.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_ruff_ratchet.py` iterates every `tool.ruff.lint.per-file-ignores` code and fails if the code equals `RUF` or starts with `RUF`.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The implementation records the post-remediation per-code RUF census on this ticket, including the authoritative RUF100 result from `ruff check src tests`.\n- [ ] `make lint` exits 0.\n- [ ] `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -q` exits 0.\n\n<!-- green-on-origin-main AC -->\n- [ ] After `git fetch origin`, `ruff check --select RUF --ignore RUF001,RUF002,RUF003,RUF100 src/rebar tests` and `make lint` exit 0 against the **current** `origin/main`; any pre-existing RUF diagnostic on current `origin/main` (including drift-introduced since the measured commit) is resolved before the RUF ratchet is landed.\n","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"Enable RUF with explicit RUF001-003 deferral"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ruff_ratchet.py","reason":"Pin the approved RUF configuration"},{"path":"src/rebar","reason":"Clear production RUF100 and approved RUF findings"},{"path":"tests","reason":"Clear test-tree RUF100 and approved RUF findings"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on